  working on  the deep clip website so and i just want  to thank you for your attention and  uh and i'm happy to uh to answer  questions  thank you thomas for your informative  presentation  we will now start the live q a portion  of the webinar  if you have a question you would like to  ask please do so now  just click on the ask a question box  located on the far  left of your screen we'll answer as many  questions as we have time for  let's get started our first question is  could this solution be used for  sequencing alignment or sequencing  comparison for instance  okay so uh thank you for the question um  that's not  something that we've considered much uh  i suppose  in if you're looking at cross species  comparisons  and looking for uh for uh conservation  not so much of the sequence but of the  uh of the regulation so that could be  binding of  proteins to particular exons and  regulation that  might not be appear immediately  recognizable just from that sequence  alone  and then using these uh protein binding  models could give you some clues about  uh more functional conservation that  sequencing conservation  but we haven't really we haven't really  thought about using it for uh for  sequencing alignment  okay thank you thomas our next question  is  how long can my sequences be or how  short  yeah so so i've talked about this long  prediction mode and that's where we use  this sliding window algorithm  uh and and we trained uh all of these  models with a max  model maximum input size of 75  nucleotides  and a minimum size of 12 nucleotides so  so  in the range of that you will you will  get the single  you get the binding profile you will get  the single prediction score  uh but if you're using longer sequences  than that then you have to use this  sliding window window algorithm to  produce a binding profile  and that does not produce an overall  prediction scores because that becomes  less and less meaningful  you can actually use very short input  you